    0752 974F 303C 1E0B 2F91 4A06 7950 BE13 52DC 8C8B

Before trusting this key, verify that the fingerprint above matches
the fingerprint published through an independent, trusted source.
Do not rely solely on a copy of this file obtained from the same
location as the release, as that source may have been compromised.

Importing the key
-----------------

To import this key into your GnuPG keyring:

    gpg --import KEYS

After importing it, verify the fingerprint:

    gpg --fingerprint 7950BE1352DC8C8B

Confirm that the fingerprint is:

    0752 974F 303C 1E0B 2F91 4A06 7950 BE13 52DC 8C8B

Verifying a release
-------------------

Official release artifacts are accompanied by OpenPGP signatures.

For example, to verify an AppImage:

    gpg --verify acLife_0.0.1_amd64.AppImage.asc acLife_0.0.1_amd64.AppImage

To verify an executable:

    gpg --verify aclife-desktop.asc aclife-desktop

A successful verification should report <Good signature> and identify
the signer as acLife Release <aclife@atrxis.com>.

Note that a valid signature only establishes that the artifact was
signed by the corresponding private key. You should verify the key's
fingerprint through a trusted, independent source before relying on
the signature.

